For production CMMS/ERP, the strongest new feature is:
Vendor Contract, Compliance & Performance Management
This turns vendor from a simple master record into a real operational/vendor-control module.
Highest Impact Features
Vendor onboarding and approval workflow
New vendors should not become usable immediately. Flow:
DRAFT -> SUBMITTED -> UNDER_REVIEW -> APPROVED -> ACTIVE -> SUSPENDED -> BLACKLISTED
Store GST/tax details, company registration, contact persons, bank/payment details, service categories, supported sites, approval history.

Contract and SLA management
Add vendor contracts per client/site/category:
response time, resolution time, working hours, emergency support, penalty rules, contract start/end date, renewal reminder.
Example:
emergency breakdown vendor must respond within 2 hours for Site A, but within 6 hours for Site B.

Vendor compliance documents
Track documents with expiry:
insurance, safety certificate, labor license, NDA, GST/tax certificate, ISO certificate, work permit eligibility.
Block assignment if required compliance is expired.

Vendor qualification by site and service
Current vendor site assignment is basic. Production should support:
site, service category, equipment category, skill/certification, contract coverage, priority vendor, backup vendor.
Example:
Vendor A can repair compressors at Chennai site, but not electrical panels.

Vendor performance scorecard
Auto-calculate:
average response time, average resolution time, SLA breaches, repeat failures, first-time-fix rate, rejected work count, safety incidents, cost variance.
This helps procurement and maintenance teams decide renewals.

Vendor work order / external service flow
For outsourced work:
assignment created -> vendor accepts -> technician visits -> work proof uploaded -> supervisor verifies -> invoice allowed.
Add vendor acknowledgement and vendor completion submission.

Vendor portal
External vendors can log in and only see their assigned jobs. They can:
accept/reject job, update ETA, upload photos, add service report, request spares, submit invoice.

Quotation and rate card
For non-contract jobs:
request quotation from multiple vendors, compare price/ETA/warranty, approve one vendor, convert to assignment or purchase request.

Invoice and payment matching
Match vendor invoice against:
work order, contract rate, spare usage, approved completion, penalties, taxes.
This is important for ERP integration.

Multi-client vendor isolation
   Since multiple clients will use the ERP, vendor records may need tenant/client ownership:
   global vendor, client-specific vendor, site-specific approval, client-specific contract terms.

   Same vendor may be approved for one client and blocked for another.
